-- title:
--   Lifting functions regular off the ends from an affine chart, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$ (`hq2`), let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$ (`hqM'`), and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$ (`hℓ`, `hℓ12`, `hℓM'`). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`). Write $\overline{F}_{M'}$ for `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the subfield of the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, and $F$ for `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding field at level $q^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ (the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$); the hypothesis `hle` asserts $\overline{F}_{M'}\subseteq F$.
--
--   On the characteristic-$p$ side, let `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` be the subfield of the Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of this field over the residue field of $A$, and let `hW` assert that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is, the places $w$ which are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value at the generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ from $\overline{F}_{M'}$ to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\overline{F}_{M'}$ together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the characteristic-$p$ field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and its residue field, together with a place map and its degree and order compatibilities). The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that $R_0$ compute reductions coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\overline{F}_{M'}$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and the Laurent series attached to its $R_0$-residue equals the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Finally, let $s\in W$ be one of the supersingular places.
--
--   Let $F_{ss}$ be a field that is an algebra over the residue field of $A$, and let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ from $F$ to $F_{ss}$, i.e. a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ with a surjective residue map onto $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, meeting $A$ correctly on constants and admitting, for each nonzero $f\in F$, a scaling $c\cdot f$ with nonzero residue. Let $N$ be a finite set of places of $F_{ss}$ over the residue field of $A$ (the ends), and, for each place $Q$ of $F_{ss}$, let $S_Q$ be a subring of $F$, $\varphi_Q\colon A[X]\to S_Q$ and $\chi_{0,Q}\colon S_Q\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ ring homomorphisms, and $D_Q$ a set of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   The hypotheses on these data are: `h0`, that $F_{ss}$ contains an element transcendental over the residue field of $A$; `h1`, the compatibility of $R$ with $R_0$ at $s$, namely that for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which is regular at every place $P$ of $\overline{F}_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue is the image in $F_{ss}$ of the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$; `h2`, that $R.\mathrm{integers}$ is stable under every $\operatorname{levelAutBar} q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense that its preimage under this automorphism is itself; and `hcard`, that $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   The hypothesis `hpkg` provides, for every place $Q\notin N$, a smooth-point package with fourteen clauses: the image of $A$ in $F$ lies in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ in $F$ and $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$, for all $a\in A$; $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(X))=0$; for every $c\in A$ with zero residue there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi\colon S_Q\to A$ with $\chi(\varphi_Q(C\,a))=a$ for all $a$, with residue equal to $\chi_{0,Q}$, and with $\chi(\varphi_Q(X))=c$; every $f\in S_Q$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there is the image of $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$ in the residue field of $Q$; $\varphi_Q(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and the order of its $R$-residue at $Q$ is $1$; $D_Q$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ of $F$ such that every $f\in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$, and such that $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $<1$ precisely when $\chi_{0,Q}(f)=0$; every $\chi\colon S_Q\to A$ that is the identity on constants and has residue $\chi_{0,Q}$ is realised by a unique $P\in D_Q$ via $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f=\chi(f)$; for $P\in D_Q$, an element $f\in F$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ exactly when $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in S_Q$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,h\neq 0$; a unit principle, that a nonzero $f\in F$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f=0$ for all $P\in D_Q$ becomes, after multiplication by a nonzero constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a unit of $S_Q$; and, conversely, that any $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ lying in the valuation subring of every $P\in D_Q$ belongs to $S_Q$.
--
--   Further: `hdisj`, that the discs $D_Q$ for distinct $Q\notin N$ are disjoint; `hcusp`, that every $P\in D_Q$ with $Q\notin N$ satisfies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image in $F$ of the $q$-expansion `jq`; `heqv`, that for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms of $F$ generated by the $\operatorname{levelAutBar} q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ of $F_{ss}$ preserves $N$ setwise and carries the discs along, $\operatorname{smulDisc}\tau\,(D_Q)=D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q}$ for $Q\notin N$; `hUniq`, that for $Q\notin N$ the package is unique, in that any quadruple $(S,\varphi,\chi_0,D)$ satisfying the same fourteen clauses has $D=D_Q$, $S=S_Q$ and $\chi_0=\chi_{0,Q}$ on common elements; and `hdl`, the Drinfeld identification: for any algebra structure of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ on the residue field of $A$, any witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and any primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ and an isomorphism $e$ of $F_{ss}$ over the residue field of $A$ with the fixed field [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q (ResidueField A) Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) such that $\#C_s=\operatorname{placeWidthChar} q\,M'\,s$ — the quantity `jWidthChar q` of the value of $s$ at `jGeomGen` divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`, the numerator being $12$ or $1$ for $q=2$ according as that value is $0$ or not — and such that, for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\operatorname{redQ} q\,\gamma,1)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) and $\operatorname{levelAutBar} q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the map $e$ intertwines the residual automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ of that level automorphism with the Drinfeld action `hFunctionFieldAction` of $(\operatorname{redQ} q\,\gamma,1)$.
--
--   The last hypothesis, `haff`, is the affine chart: there is a subring $B$ of $F$ such that the image of $A$ in $F$ lies in $B$; every element of $B$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$; $B\subseteq S_Q$ for every $Q\notin N$; and every $z\in F_{ss}$ that lies in the valuation subring of every $Q\notin N$ is the $R$-residue of some element of $B$.
--
--   The conclusion is that for every $z\in F_{ss}$ lying in the valuation subring of every place $Q\notin N$ there exist $g\in F$ and a proof that $g\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ such that the $R$-residue of $g$ is $z$, and such that for every $Q\notin N$ and every $P\in D_Q$ one has $g$ in the valuation subring of $P$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,g\in A$.
--
--   This is the lifting step in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ along its supersingular component: a function on the special fibre that is regular away from the $q+1$ ends is lifted to a function integral for the regular prolongation $R$ which is moreover regular, with values in $A$, at every point of every smooth residue disc. It is the $q=2$ form of the statement, under the rigidity guard provided by a prime $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$ and with the count $\#C_s$ equal to `placeWidthChar`, and it is used to produce generators of the chart in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_exists_generators_regular_off_ends_of_affineChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_exists_generators_regular_off_ends_of_affineChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
